{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to the measured diagnosis: the 75-event compaction's hold time is **488.2s (8m08s)**, not the '>20 minutes, still holding' I recorded while the run was in flight. My liveness check was `pgrep -f 'rebar_probe.py compact'`, whose pattern matched my own shell command line, so it reported RUNNING after the compactor had already exited. The instrumented figure is authoritative:\n\n    {\"argv\": [\"compact\", \"6118-8fb2-774f-4c5c\"], \"site\": \"compact.py:178:_compact_locked\",\n     \"wait_s\": 0.0004, \"hold_s\": 488.2131, \"outcome\": \"ok\"}\n\n488.2s for 75 foldable events is 6.5s/event, which matches the per-event `resolve_event_commit` cost measured independently (6.23s ticket-scoped) and confirms the model: compaction hold time is `S x ~6.5s` plus ~0.4s of actual mutation, with S the number of signed folded events.\n\nNothing else in the diagnosis changes — in particular the contention result stands exactly as recorded: during that 488s hold, 6 of 6 concurrent `rebar comment` writers failed at 60s and all six writes were permanently lost. 488s against a 60s budget means an 8x overrun, so every writer arriving in the first ~7 minutes of that window loses its write. The field 2m17s gap already on this ticket is the same phenomenon at a smaller S."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786116085549422001,"uuid":"5995adf0-b23c-449c-ae41-d1cda35f88d8"}